    cmb: 19,
    cmd: 30,
    environment: "temperate mountains",
    description: "Though he draws other bugbears to follow him by his charismatic presence, a bugbear tyrant truly makes his legend by defeating and torturing other creatures. Bugbears care far less about gaining territory or forcing surrender than they do about inflicting pain and collecting heads. They’re quick to recognize and appreciate the cruelty in an antipaladin’s heart, and the supernatural ability to inflict pain on others that he brings to bear.\n\nThe tyrant doesn’t reserve his violence for enemies of the bugbear race. It doesn’t take much for him to turn on his underlings and slice them up for fun, especially if he’s growing bored.Creatures in \"Bugbear\" Category\nName CR Bugbear2Bugbear Ambusher10Bugbear Bloodmage11Bugbear Cultist7Bugbear Flesh Glutton8Bugbear Gnasher4Bugbear Lurker8Bugbear Shadow Sneak10Bugbear Stalker5Bugbear Tyrant13Bugbear\nThis dark-furred creature raises a spiked morningstar, its tiny, milk-white eyes glittering with the thrill of the coming kill.",
