    description: "A crocodile is a primeval reptile that dwells in swamps or along the banks of rivers, a habitat that often puts it in violent contact with unsuspecting prey that come to the water’s edge to drink.\n\nThe typical crocodile is 14 feet long and weighs 1,400 pounds, but larger species exist. You can use these statistics for similar creatures, such as alligators.Creatures in \"Crocodile\" Category\nName CR Crocodile2Dire Crocodile9Hetkoshu12",
